    "what_it_suggests": "the concentration of the trailing directions on rows outside the core is a general property of these Jacobians -- it is present on both axes -- but it is LARGER on the width axis, and largest at the narrow-to-mid windows where the rank is actually climbing rather than at the widest windows where it has saturated at four",
